Z||000003||mblackwell||05-30-2001||01:52 PM||||You can probably do it by editing your hosts file.  Next time you see the add, right-click on it to find it's address.  Then open your hosts file.  It will be in C:\windows.  Open it with notedpad and you should see this<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>127.0.0.1 localhost<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your computer looks at this file to resolve hostnames before it looks to DNS servers.  You can block any server you want by setting its IP address incorrectly in this file.  So after you find the address of the server that the monkey ad is on, add a new line to the hosts file.  Example:<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>www.dumbmonkey.com 127.0.0.1<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your browser will try to load the ad from your computer instead of from the actual ad server.  OF course, the add won't be there, so you will get a box with a red x in it instead of the annoying ad.<P>You have to restart the computer for the change ot take affect.<p>[This message has been edited by mblackwell (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
